# Generated data. A single 300k-frame shard set is ~3.7 GB - never commit it.
data/
*.pixels
*.meta

# Exception: the self-check fixture. 40 real frames from the real writer, 491 KB
# raw and ~5 KB once git packs them. It is the only reason `python -m mirage.data`
# (F-8) and `python -m mirage.validator` (F-9) can run in a clone that has never
# generated anything. Keep it narrow - one directory, two extensions.
!mirage/fixtures/shards/*.pixels
!mirage/fixtures/shards/*.meta

# Model artifacts and caches. Content-addressed names mean these are always
# reproducible from a config hash; see docs/world_model_architecture.md.
*.pt
tokens_*.bin

# NOT ignored: runs.jsonl. It is the E-5 append-only lab notebook, hand-authored,
# and belongs in version control. Do not add a *.jsonl rule here.

# C++ / CMake. The build-dir rules are not enough on their own: a manual
# `cl main.cpp` in sim/ drops its artifacts one level above them, which is
# how 11.8 MB of them reached the index once already.
build/
build-*/
build-asan/
*.o
*.so
*.a
*.exe
*.obj
*.ilk
*.pdb

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# MuJoCo writes this next to the working directory on every run, whether or
# not anything failed. It was tracked once, holding one line from a
# deliberate bad-scene test.
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT

# Tooling
wandb/
.vscode/

# Claude Code worktrees. EnterWorktree creates linked checkouts here; an
# unignored worktree dir commits an entire second copy of the tree.
.claude/worktrees/
